{"id": "EUVD-2018-21963", "enisaUuid": "3d8e7fb8-edb1-3e67-b320-9c8ba053cd4d", "description": "MetInfo CMS 6.0.0 before 6.1.1 contains a path traversal vulnerability in /include/thumb.php that allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files via the dir parameter. Attackers can send crafted requests with backslash sequences bypassing the str_replace filter to read files like config_db.php on Windows. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-14.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:26", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://web.archive.org/web/20190916061234/https://paper.seebug.org/676/", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/other/metinfo-lfi.yaml", "https://www.metinfo.cn/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/metinfo-cms-6.1.1-unauthenticated-path-traversal-via-thumb-php-dir-parameter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f89h-c9q7-hw4h", "CVE-2018-25439"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d73e531c-5865-3f87-9d17-fc7d7581dcec", "product": {"name": "MetInfo", "vendor": {"name": "MetInfo"}}, "product_version": "6.0.0 <6.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5e7fd6e1-b6c5-3ad7-8893-e77b850defb2", "vendor": {"name": "MetInfo"}}], "isExploited": false}